---A detail for a distro and package affected by this vulnerability and its associated fix (if one is available).
---@class gcp.containeranalysis_v1.Detail
---@field packageType? string The type of package; whether native or non native (e.g., ruby gems, node.js packages, etc.).
---@field fixedCpeUri? string The distro recommended [CPE URI](https://cpe.mitre.org/specification/) to update to that contains a fix for this vulnerability. It is possible for this to be different from the affected_cpe_uri.
---@field affectedVersionEnd? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.Version The version number at the end of an interval in which this vulnerability exists. A vulnerability can affect a package between version numbers that are disjoint sets of intervals (example: [1.0.0-1.1.0], [2.4.6-2.4.8] and [4.5.6-4.6.8]) each of which will be represented in its own Detail. If a specific affected version is provided by a vulnerability database, affected_version_start and affected_version_end will be the same in that Detail.
---@field isObsolete? boolean Whether this detail is obsolete. Occurrences are expected not to point to obsolete details.
---@field source? string The source from which the information in this Detail was obtained.
---@field affectedPackage? string Required. The package this vulnerability affects.
---@field description? string A vendor-specific description of this vulnerability.
---@field severityName? string The distro assigned severity of this vulnerability.
---@field affectedCpeUri? string Required. The [CPE URI](https://cpe.mitre.org/specification/) this vulnerability affects.
---@field fixedPackage? string The distro recommended package to update to that contains a fix for this vulnerability. It is possible for this to be different from the affected_package.
---@field vendor? string The name of the vendor of the product.
---@field affectedVersionStart? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.Version The version number at the start of an interval in which this vulnerability exists. A vulnerability can affect a package between version numbers that are disjoint sets of intervals (example: [1.0.0-1.1.0], [2.4.6-2.4.8] and [4.5.6-4.6.8]) each of which will be represented in its own Detail. If a specific affected version is provided by a vulnerability database, affected_version_start and affected_version_end will be the same in that Detail.
---@field sourceUpdateTime? string The time this information was last changed at the source. This is an upstream timestamp from the underlying information source - e.g. Ubuntu security tracker.
---@field fixedVersion? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.Version The distro recommended version to update to that contains a fix for this vulnerability. Setting this to VersionKind.MAXIMUM means no such version is yet available.

