---The Upgrade Distribution represents metadata about the Upgrade for each operating system (CPE). Some distributions have additional metadata around updates, classifying them into various categories and severities.
---@class gcp.containeranalysis_v1.UpgradeDistribution
---@field cve? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.StringList The cve tied to this Upgrade.
---@field cpeUri? string Required - The specific operating system this metadata applies to. See https://cpe.mitre.org/specification/.
---@field classification? string The operating system classification of this Upgrade, as specified by the upstream operating system upgrade feed. For Windows the classification is one of the category_ids listed at https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/previous-versions/windows/desktop/ff357803(v=vs.85)
---@field severity? string The severity as specified by the upstream operating system.

---@alias gcp.containeranalysis_v1.UpgradeDistributionList gcp.containeranalysis_v1.UpgradeDistribution[]

---An Upgrade Note represents a potential upgrade of a package to a given version. For each package version combination (i.e. bash 4.0, bash 4.1, bash 4.1.2), there will be an Upgrade Note. For Windows, windows_update field represents the information related to the update.
---@class gcp.containeranalysis_v1.UpgradeNote
---@field package? string Required for non-Windows OS. The package this Upgrade is for.
---@field version? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.Version Required for non-Windows OS. The version of the package in machine + human readable form.
---@field windowsUpdate? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.WindowsUpdate Required for Windows OS. Represents the metadata about the Windows update.
---@field distributions? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.UpgradeDistributionList Metadata about the upgrade for each specific operating system.

---An Upgrade Occurrence represents that a specific resource_url could install a specific upgrade. This presence is supplied via local sources (i.e. it is present in the mirror and the running system has noticed its availability). For Windows, both distribution and windows_update contain information for the Windows update.
---@class gcp.containeranalysis_v1.UpgradeOccurrence
---@field windowsUpdate? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.WindowsUpdate Required for Windows OS. Represents the metadata about the Windows update.
---@field package? string Required for non-Windows OS. The package this Upgrade is for.
---@field distribution? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.UpgradeDistribution Metadata about the upgrade for available for the specific operating system for the resource_url. This allows efficient filtering, as well as making it easier to use the occurrence.
---@field parsedVersion? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.Version Required for non-Windows OS. The version of the package in a machine + human readable form.

---Version contains structured information about the version of a package.
---@class gcp.containeranalysis_v1.Version
---@field fullName? string Human readable version string. This string is of the form :- and is only set when kind is NORMAL.
---@field revision? string The iteration of the package build from the above version.
---@field kind? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.VersionKindEnum|string Required. Distinguishes between sentinel MIN/MAX versions and normal versions.
---@field inclusive? boolean Whether this version is specifying part of an inclusive range. Grafeas does not have the capability to specify version ranges; instead we have fields that specify start version and end versions. At times this is insufficient - we also need to specify whether the version is included in the range or is excluded from the range. This boolean is expected to be set to true when the version is included in a range.
---@field epoch? number Used to correct mistakes in the version numbering scheme.
---@field name? string Required only when version kind is NORMAL. The main part of the version name.

---@alias gcp.containeranalysis_v1.VersionKindEnum "VERSION_KIND_UNSPECIFIED"|"NORMAL"|"MINIMUM"|"MAXIMUM"

---VexAssessment provides all publisher provided Vex information that is related to this vulnerability.
---@class gcp.containeranalysis_v1.VexAssessment
---@field cve? string Holds the MITRE standard Common Vulnerabilities and Exposures (CVE) tracking number for the vulnerability. Deprecated: Use vulnerability_id instead to denote CVEs.
---@field relatedUris? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.RelatedUrlList Holds a list of references associated with this vulnerability item and assessment.
---@field remediations? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.RemediationList Specifies details on how to handle (and presumably, fix) a vulnerability.
---@field state? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.VexAssessmentStateEnum|string Provides the state of this Vulnerability assessment.
---@field justification? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.Justification Justification provides the justification when the state of the assessment if NOT_AFFECTED.
---@field vulnerabilityId? string The vulnerability identifier for this Assessment. Will hold one of common identifiers e.g. CVE, GHSA etc.
---@field noteName? string The VulnerabilityAssessment note from which this VexAssessment was generated. This will be of the form: `projects/[PROJECT_ID]/notes/[NOTE_ID]`.
---@field impacts? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.StringList Contains information about the impact of this vulnerability, this will change with time.

---@alias gcp.containeranalysis_v1.VexAssessmentStateEnum "STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"AFFECTED"|"NOT_AFFECTED"|"FIXED"|"UNDER_INVESTIGATION"

---A single VulnerabilityAssessmentNote represents one particular product's vulnerability assessment for one CVE.
---@class gcp.containeranalysis_v1.VulnerabilityAssessmentNote
---@field assessment? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.Assessment Represents a vulnerability assessment for the product.
---@field longDescription? string A detailed description of this Vex.
---@field product? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.Product The product affected by this vex.
---@field publisher? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.Publisher Publisher details of this Note.
---@field shortDescription? string A one sentence description of this Vex.
---@field languageCode? string Identifies the language used by this document, corresponding to IETF BCP 47 / RFC 5646.
---@field title? string The title of the note. E.g. `Vex-Debian-11.4`

---A security vulnerability that can be found in resources.
---@class gcp.containeranalysis_v1.VulnerabilityNote
---@field advisoryPublishTime? string The time this advisory was published by the source.
---@field windowsDetails? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.WindowsDetailList Windows details get their own format because the information format and model don't match a normal detail. Specifically Windows updates are done as patches, thus Windows vulnerabilities really are a missing package, rather than a package being at an incorrect version.
---@field cvssV3? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.CVSSv3 The full description of the CVSSv3 for this vulnerability.
---@field cvssV4? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.CVSS The full description of the v4 CVSS for this vulnerability.
---@field cvssScore? number The CVSS score of this vulnerability. CVSS score is on a scale of 0 - 10 where 0 indicates low severity and 10 indicates high severity.
---@field cvssV2? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.CVSS The full description of the v2 CVSS for this vulnerability.
---@field details? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.DetailList Details of all known distros and packages affected by this vulnerability.
---@field sourceUpdateTime? string The time this information was last changed at the source. This is an upstream timestamp from the underlying information source - e.g. Ubuntu security tracker.
---@field cvssVersion? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.VulnerabilityNoteCvssVersionEnum|string CVSS version used to populate cvss_score and severity.
---@field severity? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.VulnerabilityNoteSeverityEnum|string The note provider assigned severity of this vulnerability.

---@alias gcp.containeranalysis_v1.VulnerabilityNoteCvssVersionEnum "CVSS_VERSION_UNSPECIFIED"|"CVSS_VERSION_2"|"CVSS_VERSION_3"|"CVSS_VERSION_4"

---@alias gcp.containeranalysis_v1.VulnerabilityNoteSeverityEnum "SEVERITY_UNSPECIFIED"|"MINIMAL"|"LOW"|"MEDIUM"|"HIGH"|"CRITICAL"

---An occurrence of a severity vulnerability on a resource.
---@class gcp.containeranalysis_v1.VulnerabilityOccurrence
---@field fixAvailable? boolean Output only. Whether at least one of the affected packages has a fix available.
---@field packageIssue? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.PackageIssueList Required. The set of affected locations and their fixes (if available) within the associated resource.
---@field cvssScore? number Output only. The CVSS score of this vulnerability. CVSS score is on a scale of 0 - 10 where 0 indicates low severity and 10 indicates high severity.
---@field cvssv3? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.CVSS The cvss v3 score for the vulnerability.
---@field relatedUrls? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.RelatedUrlList Output only. URLs related to this vulnerability.
---@field cvssVersion? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.VulnerabilityOccurrenceCvssVersionEnum|string Output only. CVSS version used to populate cvss_score and severity.
---@field type? string The type of package; whether native or non native (e.g., ruby gems, node.js packages, etc.).
---@field exploitability? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.Exploitability Output only. Rollup of exploitability across all PackageIssues in this occurrence.
---@field risk? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.Risk Risk information about the vulnerability, such as CISA, EPSS, etc.
---@field shortDescription? string Output only. A one sentence description of this vulnerability.
---@field extraDetails? string Occurrence-specific extra details about the vulnerability.
---@field cvssV4? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.CVSS The cvss v4 score for the vulnerability.
---@field severity? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.VulnerabilityOccurrenceSeverityEnum|string Output only. The note provider assigned severity of this vulnerability.
---@field longDescription? string Output only. A detailed description of this vulnerability.
---@field effectiveSeverity? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.VulnerabilityOccurrenceEffectiveSeverityEnum|string The distro assigned severity for this vulnerability when it is available, otherwise this is the note provider assigned severity. When there are multiple PackageIssues for this vulnerability, they can have different effective severities because some might be provided by the distro while others are provided by the language ecosystem for a language pack. For this reason, it is advised to use the effective severity on the PackageIssue level. In the case where multiple PackageIssues have differing effective severities, this field should be the highest severity for any of the PackageIssues.
---@field cvssV2? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.CVSS The cvss v2 score for the vulnerability.
---@field vexAssessment? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.VexAssessment

---@alias gcp.containeranalysis_v1.VulnerabilityOccurrenceCvssVersionEnum "CVSS_VERSION_UNSPECIFIED"|"CVSS_VERSION_2"|"CVSS_VERSION_3"|"CVSS_VERSION_4"

---@alias gcp.containeranalysis_v1.VulnerabilityOccurrenceEffectiveSeverityEnum "SEVERITY_UNSPECIFIED"|"MINIMAL"|"LOW"|"MEDIUM"|"HIGH"|"CRITICAL"

---@alias gcp.containeranalysis_v1.VulnerabilityOccurrenceSeverityEnum "SEVERITY_UNSPECIFIED"|"MINIMAL"|"LOW"|"MEDIUM"|"HIGH"|"CRITICAL"

---A summary of how many vulnerability occurrences there are per resource and severity type.
---@class gcp.containeranalysis_v1.VulnerabilityOccurrencesSummary
---@field unreachable? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.StringList Unordered list. Unreachable regions. Populated for requests from the global region when `return_partial_success` is set. Format: `projects/[PROJECT_ID]/locations/[LOCATION]`
---@field counts? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.FixableTotalByDigestList A listing by resource of the number of fixable and total vulnerabilities.

---@class gcp.containeranalysis_v1.WindowsDetail
---@field description? string The description of this vulnerability.
---@field name? string Required. The name of this vulnerability.
---@field cpeUri? string Required. The [CPE URI](https://cpe.mitre.org/specification/) this vulnerability affects.
---@field fixingKbs? gcp.containeranalysis_v1.KnowledgeBaseList Required. The names of the KBs which have hotfixes to mitigate this vulnerability. Note that there may be multiple hotfixes (and thus multiple KBs) that mitigate a given vulnerability. Currently any listed KBs presence is considered a fix.

---@alias gcp.containeranalysis_v1.WindowsDetailList gcp.containeranalysis_v1.WindowsDetail[]

